alta: make hw_job_limit writable at runtime, trip to 1 after a recovered hang

hw_job_limit (how many jobs may sit in the NPU's hardware ring at once) was
read-only and fixed at module load. Now it can be written at any time
(1-4, /sys/module/etnaviv/parameters/hw_job_limit). The scheduler's credit
pool is fixed at 12 and every job asks for 12 / limit credits through the
scheduler's update_job_credits hook, so lowering the limit never trips the
credit underflow warning, and the change applies as the ring drains.

hw_job_auto (default on): a hang or MMU fault the driver recovers from sets
hw_job_limit to 1 until someone writes it again; hw_job_trips counts these
and hw_job_trip_from holds the limit before the last one, for a desktop tool
that warns the user and offers to put it back or reboot.

hw_job_turns (default off): jobs from different DRM files (programs) never
share the ring. Off, programs share it as in stock etnaviv.

Logs "alta: hw_job_limit N (writable, 1-4), hw_job_auto on, hw_job_turns off"
at load and "alta: hw_job_limit N -> 1 after a recovered hang" on a trip.
Applies on top of 0001-0005; touches etnaviv_sched.c and etnaviv_gpu.h only.

